{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony","id":707529,"title":"Seeking a More Mobile Harmony","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-18T15:17:36-07:00","id":707529,"title":"Seeking a More Mobile Harmony","content":"So has anyone else noticed that moving Harmony tends to get really difficult? If you average one success on three dice, then you only tend to occasionally move Harmony unless you go out and just, like, eat your way through a crowd or go live in the Shadow for a while.<br /> <br /> One of the interesting things I noticed was that if you're already away from the middle, it's easier to go to that pole. I think, for some reason, this should have been reversed. If a werewolf is a creature of balance, then being at one end of the spectrum should make it easier to go to the -opposite- end of the spectrum. For instance, a spirit breaking point for someone at Harmony 10 should be a pretty big deal, and the system should make it hard to stay there. But that's not the way it seems to actually work.<br /> <br /> So, has anyone tinkered with Harmony any to try and make it more... well, mobile? If a werewolf's Harmony is supposed to be constantly shifting, then the system should reflect that, I think. As it stands, it tends to favor staying right where you are.<br /> <br /> Who else has seen this? What have you done about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:29:13-07:00","id":707588,"title":"","content":"Generally if you add the modifiers you'll move around faster.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that werewolves are not creatures of balance, balance is something you might strive for, and different werewolves are going to consider different parts of Harmony ideal.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, it's like Beats. It's meant to promote action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-18-2015, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:47:45-07:00","id":707597,"title":"","content":"I'm about 99% sure that werewolves tending to drift away from harmony once they get unbalanced is entirely intentional on the part of the designers.<br /> <br /> It's &quot;supposed&quot; to do exactly what it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T10:00:36-07:00","id":710838,"title":"","content":"Killing a kid who's empowering some kind of negative spirit? I'm looking at -3 on the spirit breakpoint (think Columbine).<br /> <br /> Achieving perfect balance while averting a mass shooting? Priceless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T10:19:42-07:00","id":907705,"title":"","content":"The possible variant is to make all triggers open to you when you're Harmony 5. But when you move towards Flesh, some triggers toward Spirit close for you. And the more you rise your Harmony toward Flesh, the less triggers toward Spirit can affect you (until the only way for you is to eat wolf or human). The same is true for moving toward Spirit. Then Flesh-triggers cease (until the onlyway for you is to violate the Moon Oath).<br /> <br /> Also as for dice rolled. The idea is following: When your Harmony is high, it's hard to resist breaking points toward Flesh, and easy toward Spirit. And vice versa. As following:<br /> Harmony 9 -- 1 Die to Resist Flesh-Triggers -- 5 Dice to resist Spirit-Triggers<br /> Harmony 7-8 -- 2 Dice to Resist Flesh-Triggers -- 4 Dice to resist Spirit-Triggers<br /> Harmony 4-6 -- 3 Dice to Resist Flesh-Triggers -- 3 Dice to resist Spirit-Triggers<br /> Harmony 2-3 -- 4 Dice to Resist Flesh-Triggers -- 2 Dice to resist Spirit-Triggers<br /> Harmony 1 -- 5 Dice to Resist Flesh-Triggers -- 1 Die to resist Spirit-Triggers<br /> <br /> Then itwill be hard to stick to the middle, but all too easy to fall in either direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-05-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:37:31-07:00","id":908744,"title":"","content":"I agree that moving Harmony seems pretty difficult and not at all frequent, but I can't decide whether I like that or not. As nofather said, Uratha aren't creatures of balance; they're creatures <i>striving</i> for balance, and I feel that both more-mobile Harmony and less-mobile Harmony have pros and cons.<br /> <br /> My concern is that (unless I'm reading it wrong), there aren't <i>actually any minuses to Breaking Point rolls</i> if you're sitting at Harmony 5. To me, that feels a little wrong - although slipping further from balance once you've started on that route is indeed very thematic, it feels (imo) <i>against theme</i> to have <i>the least chance of Breaking at Balance</i>. Sittin' pretty at Harmony 5 should NEVER last long in WtF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":2653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","user":"NateD","date":". 06-06-2016, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:47:27-07:00","id":908784,"title":"","content":"I'd almost feel like if you stay at harmony 5 for a while you've got being a werewolf down. Though if you're going from 7 into a rapid decline then you should just bypass it to 4. If their actions were so extreme for a quick motion, don't give them balance. They'll still remember eating the child. And as I understand it, human flesh is addictive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:55:40-07:00","id":908790,"title":"","content":"It's so easy to get, too, considering how easy they are to kill. Unless you're sitting on a locus, human flesh is probably the easiest way to get Essence. But even a Dedicated Locus only offers<br /> <br /> What does your pack do after a battle where Essence has been used to heal and power Gifts?<br /> <br /> We were out of town in our last few sessions dealing with a vampire and the Essence just dropped like a rock and then buoyed to full up again with all the gunfire and minions. There was a dog, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2016, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T19:38:21-07:00","id":908814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=908790#post908790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does your pack do after a battle where Essence has been used to heal and power Gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Siskur Dah on the first rank 1 spirit you see, distribute that essence. It's literally one Down &amp; Dirty roll away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:02:45-07:00","id":908831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=908814#post908814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siskur Dah on the first rank 1 spirit you see, distribute that essence. It's literally one Down &amp; Dirty roll away.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be taking the sacred out of it, but even then a Rank 1 spirit is only going to have 10 Essence, maximum. Presuming it was full up and didn't spend any defending itself that's just two per werewolf, given a pack of five.<br /> <br /> Do you just do it over and over? And your Storyteller hasn't offered any response to this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2016, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:39:03-07:00","id":908853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=908831#post908831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems to be taking the sacred out of it, but even then a Rank 1 spirit is only going to have 10 Essence, maximum. Presuming it was full up and didn't spend any defending itself that's just two per werewolf, given a pack of five.<br /> <br /> Do you just do it over and over? And your Storyteller hasn't offered any response to this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wolf Must Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:50:35-07:00","id":908860,"title":"","content":"Right, well, back to the original concern, it's probably important to recognize that the Harmony chart does not depict the only Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> 'They\u2019re a starting point rather than a definitive list. The player and Storyteller should work together to define one or two breaking points in each direction for her character based on her auspice, tribe, and Touchstones. Breaking points toward Flesh involve actively denying her Uratha nature. Breaking points toward Spirit instead require her to turn her back on her heritage in the world of Flesh.'<br /> <br /> And modifiers should probably be similarly altered depending on the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:36:36-07:00","id":909188,"title":"","content":"But still the problem is that when you fall in either direction from the middle, it's all too easy to move back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:47:03-07:00","id":909195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=909188#post909188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But still the problem is that when you fall in either direction from the middle, it's all too easy to move back.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on your lifestyle and Touchstones, on what's going on. Lingering around the middle shouldn't be uncommon for a standard pack that's out there doing things. But if you're forced to lay low because of hunters or take a long journey to the spirit you should expect it to hang around the other end.<br /> <br /> What's your pack actually doing? Balancing their human life and their spiritual side? Following the Oaths and protecting their territory? Then you wouldn't expect a lot of movement away from the middle, because they're acting harmoniously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:49:09-07:00","id":909197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=909188#post909188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But still the problem is that when you fall in either direction from the middle, it's all too easy to move back.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trick isn't in swinging the pendulum the opposite direction - it's in stopping it in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T09:09:04-07:00","id":909210,"title":"","content":"One idea I have kicked around for my home game is ritualized Breaking Points, emphasizing weird, cultish behavior as a means of keeping Harmony in balance. I was originally going to make it less traumatic since the rituals are voluntary, but now I'm torn on whether I want achieving Harmony to be so easy on characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:19:59-07:00","id":909253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=909210#post909210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I have kicked around for my home game is ritualized Breaking Points, emphasizing weird, cultish behavior as a means of keeping Harmony in balance. I was originally going to make it less traumatic since the rituals are voluntary, but now I'm torn on whether I want achieving Harmony to be so easy on characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the rituals that the Pure engaged on to keep themselves sane despite basically pursuing genocide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T01:12:26-07:00","id":909911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=908814#post908814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Siskur Dah on the first rank 1 spirit you see, distribute that essence. It's literally one Down &amp; Dirty roll away.</div> </div> </div> </div>And welcome to the Predator Kings and Fire-Touched Siskur-Dah hit list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T03:17:56-07:00","id":909948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=909911#post909911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And welcome to the Predator Kings and Fire-Touched Siskur-Dah hit list.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are Blood Talons for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T04:40:37-07:00","id":909974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=909948#post909948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are Blood Talons for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dying messily.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T04:47:49-07:00","id":909976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=909974#post909974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dying messily.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *Gloriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:57:15-07:00","id":910196,"title":"","content":"&quot;Man, what a glorious mess&quot; is not an uncommon response to a scene where the Blood Talons have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T03:43:04-07:00","id":910675,"title":"","content":"None of that is to say that abusing Siskur-Dah is &quot;doing it wrong&quot; though, right? Provoking the Pure, pissing off the spirit courts, hell - even being so much of a monster that hunting and eating spirits is a *daily occurrence* for you - they're features, not bugs. Same with cannibalism, really - all of those things lead to some really interesting stories.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, not enough Essence (and, to get back to the OP, worrying too much about your Harmony) is less fun.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, in play, my problem so far has been my players not hitting ENOUGH breaking points to really dip very far down in Harmony. Maybe I just need to show them all those benefits of a...balanced diet. *boom tish*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T17:23:50-07:00","id":912543,"title":"","content":"I feel like Harmony is best when personalized to each character, I ignore some of the Breaking points because for some tribes it doesn't make sense. Iron Masters are the most tied to humanity so why are they most likely to be way too much toward spirit each time they kill their favored Prey? Doesn't make sense, applies to other Tribes too. A Blood Talon only ever gets penalized for going against the Oath when it is actual murder and not a fair fight with just cause. Otherwise both tribes would nearly be unplayable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T02:37:21-07:00","id":912705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=912543#post912543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Harmony is best when personalized to each character, I ignore some of the Breaking points because for some tribes it doesn't make sense. Iron Masters are the most tied to humanity so why are they most likely to be way too much toward spirit each time they kill their favored Prey? Doesn't make sense, applies to other Tribes too. A Blood Talon only ever gets penalized for going against the Oath when it is actual murder and not a fair fight with just cause. Otherwise both tribes would nearly be unplayable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One could argue that dealing with the spiritual consequences of their actions as a tribe is entirely thematic and that removing it guts their theme.<br /> <br /> Being at an extreme end of the Harmony track isn't unplayable. It's story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T03:19:13-07:00","id":912714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=912705#post912705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could argue that dealing with the spiritual consequences of their actions as a tribe is entirely thematic and that removing it guts their theme.<br /> <br /> Being at an extreme end of the Harmony track isn't unplayable. It's story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree to a point, but it means those tribes would be considered crazy as a whole and killing humans doesn't make sense because the book numerous times makes it clear WW don't care if they kill humans. it also means that only 3 tribes are viable to people not wanting to play very unbalanced WW and the game doesn't really prepare you for that or make it seem at all that's the case for either. Nevermind The Iron masters closeness with humanity seems a lie since they all seem way too close to spirit.<br /> <br /> Just doesn't make sense thematically","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T04:03:55-07:00","id":912726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=912714#post912714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree to a point, but it means those tribes would be considered crazy as a whole and killing humans doesn't make sense because the book numerous times makes it clear WW don't care if they kill humans. it also means that only 3 tribes are viable to people not wanting to play very unbalanced WW and the game doesn't really prepare you for that or make it seem at all that's the case for either. Nevermind The Iron masters closeness with humanity seems a lie since they all seem way too close to spirit.<br /> <br /> Just doesn't make sense thematically</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see your point, but I'm not sure we should assume that members of these tribes wouldn't routinely throw themselves into things that pull towards the other end of Harmony if they were interested in maintaining balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T04:16:23-07:00","id":912731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=912714#post912714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree to a point, but it means those tribes would be considered crazy as a whole and killing humans doesn't make sense because the book numerous times makes it clear WW don't care if they kill humans. it also means that only 3 tribes are viable to people not wanting to play very unbalanced WW and the game doesn't really prepare you for that or make it seem at all that's the case for either. Nevermind The Iron masters closeness with humanity seems a lie since they all seem way too close to spirit.<br /> <br /> Just doesn't make sense thematically</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you skipped over the part in that you don't actually need to bring your prey low literally to complete a hunt.<br /> <br /> Iron Masters make and break institutions.<br /> <br /> Successful Blood Talons demoralize the Pure so much that they will actively avoid conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T07:08:26-07:00","id":912781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=912731#post912731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose you skipped over the part in that you don't actually need to bring your prey low literally to complete a hunt.<br /> <br /> Iron Masters make and break institutions.<br /> <br /> Successful Blood Talons demoralize the Pure so much that they will actively avoid conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Plus, is it coincidence that the tribe with (arguably) easiest access to Flesh-unbalancing processed food hunts prey that unbalances them spirit side?<br /> <br /> Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T11:12:34-07:00","id":912873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=912731#post912731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose you skipped over the part in that you don't actually need to bring your prey low literally to complete a hunt.<br /> <br /> Iron Masters make and break institutions.<br /> <br /> Successful Blood Talons demoralize the Pure so much that they will actively avoid conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually loved that part and think it adds a lot to play but to act that is all they can do is limiting and a bit naive, and I will relent to say perhaps it should be kept that way for Blood talons (although, the negative modifier seems a bit much, if only because Blood talons won't think of it as breaking their oath as much as fullfilling their roles as Blood Talons, especially since demoralizing Pure is even harder than killing them, they are kinda fanatics) But I still argue that the book can't declare killing humans is no big deal and then make it a breaking point. <br /> <br /> I mean the Book itself encourages us to seek breaking points that suit that character, and i think making the points fine tuned to character when otherwise it may not make sense is a good idea. Maybe my love for Promethean is showing through, but i like the idea of what draws you closer to spirituality or humanity being individualized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T11:18:01-07:00","id":912876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/707529-seeking-a-more-mobile-harmony?p=912873#post912873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I still argue that the book can't declare killing humans is no big deal and then make it a breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking Points for werewolves are arguably less of a big deal than they are for other games. No Beats, no chance of loss of character, they go up and down based on your in-game actions and not purchased through Experiences or long-term Aspirations. You can go through several Breaking Points in a day and be a little off-kilter but otherwise the same as when you started.<br /> <br /> It's when you take things to extremes that it becomes a big deal, or through the in-game reactions of other characters. You develop bans or more triggers, other werewolves or even humans may start hunting you. Actions bring about reactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-12-2016, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T12:00:31-07:00","id":912909,"title":"","content":"Consider, that for Uratha breaking points don't even come accompanied with relevant conditions. So, yeah, killing humans isn't a big deal for them.<br /> <br /> I've customized some things for my current character. Encouraging the spread of his totem's influence (namely: Vengeance) is a spirit breaking point for him. He did this last session by providing a gun to do as she would with a gangbanger who threatened her son.<br /> <br /> His hunt led him to this gang's hideout, where he proceeded to break over half a dozen thug's mind off Lunacy in Dalu, and break the bones of the remaining ones until he got his answers.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that his Long Term aspiration is to achieve spiritual balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-12-2016, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}